11. Phase Transitions and the Cognitive Random Energy Model

Definition 11.1 (Multi‑Term Cognitive REM). Let \mathcal{M} = \mathbb{S}^{d-1}. Define:

E(s) = -\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}} \sum_{\mu=1}^M \xi_\mu \sigma(\langle w_\mu, s \rangle) + \lambda_{\text{symb}} E_{\text{symb}}(s) + \lambda_{\text{topo}} E_{\text{topo}}(s),

where w_\mu \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I_d), \xi_\mu \sim \operatorname{Unif}(\{\pm1\}), and \sigma is a smooth sigmoid.

Theorem 11.1 (Replica‑Symmetric Free Energy). As d \to \infty with \alpha = M/d fixed, the free energy f(\beta) = -\frac{1}{\beta} \lim_{d\to\infty} \frac{1}{d} \mathbb{E} \log Z(\beta) is given, in the replica‑symmetric ansatz, by:

f(\beta) = \operatorname{extr}_{q, \hat{q}, m, \hat{m}} \left\{ \frac{\beta}{2}(1-q)^2 + \frac{\alpha}{\beta} \mathbb{E}_\xi \log \mathbb{E}_z e^{\beta \xi \sigma(\sqrt{q}z + m)} - \frac{1}{\beta} \mathbb{E}_z \log \mathbb{E}_\xi e^{\beta \xi \sigma(\sqrt{q}z + m)} + f_{\text{det}}(\lambda_{\text{symb}}, \lambda_{\text{topo}}) \right\},

where f_{\text{det}} is the deterministic contribution from the Gödel and graph‑Laplacian terms.

Proof sketch. Apply Guerra’s interpolation scheme (Talagrand, 2003; Panchenko, 2013). The interpolation parameter t \in [0,1] couples the original Hamiltonian to a reference model with known free energy. Gaussian integration by parts and the Nishimori identity yield the saddle‑point equations. The deterministic terms enter additively in the thermodynamic limit. Recent work on the Boolean SK model demonstrates that “Guerra interpolation enables the derivation of the thermodynamic limit, the replica symmetric and the broken replica free energy expressions”. ∎

Theorem 11.2 (Multiple Phase Transitions). The phase diagram exhibits at least two critical temperatures: \beta_c^{(1)} for the semantic delocalisation transition, and \beta_c^{(2)} for the logical satisfaction transition. For \beta > \max(\beta_c^{(1)}, \beta_c^{(2)}), the Gibbs measure concentrates on states that are both semantically coherent and logically admissible.

